<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  PROBE D5. NEGATIVE CONTROL for section 2.3.1's "prefer exactly one
  outputDecision per service": a <decisionService> with NO <outputDecision> at
  all, only an encapsulatedDecision.

  The reason this needs a probe rather than a reading is that the XSD does NOT
  catch it. DMN13.xsd:516 declares outputDecision with minOccurs="0", so a
  service with none is SCHEMA VALID and Xerces waves it through. Whatever
  rejects it, if anything does, is a MODEL validator, not the schema, and model
  validators are exactly what the two engines disagree about.

  What each leg is asked:
    KIE   : does kie-dmn-validation raise, and does evaluateDecisionService throw
            when there is nothing to return?
    Camunda 8 : has no service leg, so the only question is whether the malformed
            service perturbs the parse or the ordinary decisions.

  WHAT THIS DECIDES. If KIE rejects, section 2.3.1's preference is engine-backed on
  the `kie` flavor and the emitter can rely on it. If both engines are quiet, the
  emitter must guarantee the invariant itself, and a service with no output is a
  silent no-op rather than an error, which is the worse failure mode: a section
  emitted as an empty service would simply never be callable, with no diagnostic.

  MEASURED 2026-07-31, and the two engines split exactly as the probe was shaped
  to detect:
    Xerces    : VALID, as predicted from DMN13.xsd:516's minOccurs="0".
    KIE 8.44  : validator ERROR [REQ_NOT_FOUND] "Decision service 'empty' does
                not define any output decisions in top segment (outputDecision
                count: 0, encapsulatedDecision count: 1)". BUILD CLEAN. The
                ordinary decision still answers correctly. And
                evaluateDecisionService THROWS
                  java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: Kie DMN API parameter
                  'decisionIds' cannot be empty.
    Camunda 8 : completely silent. Parses, 0 errors, `step` correct. A service
                with no output is a no-op there and nothing says so.

  So section 2.3.1's preference is engine-backed on `kie` (at validate time, and
  loudly at call time) and entirely unbacked on the default flavor. Wired
  HarnessMustFail on the KIE leg and HarnessMustPass on the Camunda leg.

-->
<definitions xmlns="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/MODEL/" id="definitions_svc_no_output" name="svc_no_output" namespace="https://legalese.com/l4/dmn/svc_no_output" exporter="hand">
  <inputData id="input_n" name="n">
    <variable id="input_n_var" name="n" typeRef="number"/>
  </inputData>
  <decision id="decision_step" name="step">
    <variable id="decision_step_var" name="step" typeRef="number"/>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_step_n">
      <requiredInput href="#input_n"/>
    </informationRequirement>
    <literalExpression id="decision_step_lit">
      <text>n * 2</text>
    </literalExpression>
  </decision>
  <decisionService id="svc_empty" name="empty">
    <variable id="svc_empty_var" name="empty" typeRef="number"/>
    <encapsulatedDecision href="#decision_step"/>
    <inputData href="#input_n"/>
  </decisionService>
</definitions>
